## Source-locked tail diagnostic and D4 decision

Let

\[
\Delta_{12}=E_{20}-E_{10},\qquad
\Delta_{23}=E_{30}-E_{20}.
\]

The exact replay gives

\[
\frac{\|\Delta_{23}\|_F}{\|\Delta_{12}\|_F}
=0.2865699721044504.
\]

Every one of the 882 matched per-effect spectral increments contracts from
`D1 -> D2` to `D2 -> D3`. The increments are nevertheless strongly
anti-aligned: their cosine is `-0.8736064005996705`, and the residual of the
best scalar continuation model is `0.4866331850904622`. These facts prohibit
calling the continuation a monotone error estimate.

If the observed contraction persisted for one further rung, the forecast
`D3 -> D4` stacked relative difference would be `0.02918548300515123`, below
the inherited `0.05` threshold. The corresponding conditional post-D3
geometric tail envelope is `0.04090868321206148`. Both are empirical
diagnostics, explicitly not HEOM error bounds or convergence certificates.

For seven `K0` bath exponentials, depth four has

\[
N_{\rm ADO}(4)=\binom{7+4}{4}=330.
\]

The selected batched adjoint contains `15,620,220` complex coordinates. A
power-law fit to the measured D1, D2 and D3 runtimes forecasts
`8528.271708757764 s`, or approximately `2.37 h`; the lock reserves `5 h`.
The explicitly counted complex state requires approximately `238.35 MiB`, but
peak process memory is not certified.

All integrity, contraction and cost checks pass. The source-locked decision is
therefore

```text
D4_K0_WARRANTED_AS_ONE_LOCKED_CLASSIFICATION_RUNG
```

The D4 source lock and post-result classifier are frozen before execution. They
admit exactly three scientific exits:

1. stable effects and four bounded rows: require the predeclared K1
   cross-corner;
2. stable effects but failed bounded rows: record a stable negative result for
   this profile and change the probe or physical model;
3. unstable effects: stop blind depth escalation and test a declared hierarchy
   closure or stable-mode projection.

No D5 calculation is authorized by this packet.

This caution is consistent with the HEOM literature: finite truncations can be
uncontrolled or unstable, while projection-based closures and stable-mode
methods can be more informative than continued depth escalation. See
[Krug and Stockburger (2024)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.05520),
[Nakamura and Tanimura (2022)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.09270), and
[Dunn, Tempelaar, and Reichman (2019)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.04594).

## Boundary

Even a passing D3--D4 certificate is finite numerical support. It is not an
infinite-HEOM theorem, complete GSB/SE/ESA typing, isotropic laboratory response,
physical `K_ij`, absolute field calibration, detector covariance, physiology,
or evidence that quantum effects are necessary for life.
